    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><table class=\"wikitable\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <th><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/SHIELD_RATING\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"SHIELD RATING\">SHIELD RATING</a> </th> \n   <th>COST </th> \n   <th>UPGRADE POINT COST </th> \n   <th>AVAILABILITY </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>5 </td> \n   <td>5,000 </td> \n   <td>2 </td> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Restricted\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Restricted\">Restricted</a> </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>10 </td> \n   <td>10,000 </td> \n   <td>3 </td> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Military\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Military\">Military</a> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p>A deflector Shield Generator can be built into a suit of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medium_Armor\" title=\"Medium Armor\">Medium Armor</a> or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Armor\" title=\"Heavy Armor\">Heavy Armor</a>, giving it the same kind of protection <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Starships\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Starships\">Starships</a> and some Battle <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Droids\" title=\"Droids\">Droids</a> enjoy. Due to their bulk and power requirements, it is not possible to install anything but the smallest of Shield Generators into a suit of Armor; in fact, only <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Armor\" title=\"Heavy Armor\">Heavy Armor</a> of at least Medium size can carry a SR 10 Shield Generator. </p><p>Shield Generators operate for 10 rounds on a standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a>. (Suits of Armor with Shield Generators commonly have the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Internal_Generator\" title=\"Internal Generator\">Internal Generator</a> Upgrade.) Turning a Shield Generator on or off is a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>. When active, reduce the damage you take by the Armor's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Rating\" title=\"Shield Rating\">Shield Rating</a>. If the damage is equal to or greater than the Armor's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Rating\" title=\"Shield Rating\">Shield Rating</a>, the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Rating\" title=\"Shield Rating\">Shield Rating</a> is reduced by 5 points. By spending three <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Actions\" title=\"Swift Actions\">Swift Actions</a> on the same or consecutive rounds, the wearer can make a DC 20 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Mechanics\" title=\"Mechanics\">Mechanics</a> check to restore lost shield power. If the check succeeds, the Armor's <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Rating\" title=\"Shield Rating\">Shield Rating</a> increases by 5 points (up to its maximum <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Shield_Rating\" title=\"Shield Rating\">Shield Rating</a>). </p>",
